{title: The Four-Chord Loop}
{artist: Practice progression}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}
{difficulty: beginner}
{strumming: D - D U - U D U}
{comment: I–V–vi–IV, the progression behind a huge number of pop songs. Loop it until the changes are on the beat.}

{start_of_verse: Loop}
| G | D | Em | C |
| G | D | Em | C |
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Then try it with a capo on fret 2 using the same shapes.}
